# walk-cache.manifest - rows for the terrain walk-vs-cache check
# (tests/harness/check_terrain_walk_cache.sh); both row forms are described there.
#
#   pose row  <level> | pos=(x, y, z) yaw=Y pitch=P | [lod]
#   bk2 row   <bk2> | <VBL> | <canon|inter> | [lod]
#
# Each row is captured native-only at 16:9 twice, once through the CPU terrain
# walk and once through the retained GPU terrain cache
# (OPENPETE_TERRAIN_CACHE_FORCE=1); the differing pixel count per row is
# compared with tests/golden/spyro-2/walk-cache-baseline.tsv.
#
# Plain boot (no attract-demo.bk2: the title screen and attract demo), VBL 3973
# sub-tick present at alpha 0.5, --lod original: untextured LP faces (sector
# 96 face 5 at (357,185)), whose gouraud colour the walk and the cache agree
# on only when both stages read the vertex byte on the exact c/255 grid
# (core/rhi/shaders/psx_unorm8.glsl); off it, the pixel differs by one level
# in one channel.
attract-demo | 3973 | inter | original
#
# Near-band sub-cell keys: the drain inserts a near face's sub-cells at their
# own keys, finer than the 2x2 and the whole triangles the mesh draws, and on
# both feeds each fragment of those triangles keys and contests at the key of
# the sub-cell containing it. Close camera over near-band ground under a moby
# shadow, canonical present and the sub-tick present. The autumn-plains rows
# also hold untextured LP terrain in the upper screen, which measures the
# c/255 colour grid as the attract-demo row does.
glimmer-pogo-dialogue | 1476 | canon | original
autumn-plains-skelos-badlands-portal-entry | 1423 | canon | original
autumn-plains-skelos-badlands-portal-entry | 1423 | inter | original
# Sector 10 HP face 48 over coplanar LP faces 32/30: the walk shows HP, the
# cache shows the LP colour on 9 px at original LOD (open).
crushs_dungeon | pos=(3080, 30039, 31217) yaw=29 pitch=548 | original
